    "required_age": 0,
    "is_free": false,
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Taking inspiration from The Witness, Tunic, and many other great games, Gordian is a finely crafted puzzle game full of tricks and secrets.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Tie all 21 knots as tight as possible in order to learn about topology through the rule set Gordian uses to represent it.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Click to place rope, and then click circles to move it to adjacent tiles.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Right click to undo your last move, hold to undo more.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Earn medals by tying knots as tight as possible, which unlocks more knots for you to puzzle over.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This game can be quite a challenge at times. If you find yourself overwhelmed, your brain tied into knots, just set the game down for a bit. Don't worry, it will save your progress.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Take your time. Before you know it your brain will be solving knots in the background and you'll come back with a whole new perspective.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Controls:</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Click anywhere place the first dot, from there you may extend the rope in any of the indicated directions by clicking (or tapping) in a valid location.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Right click to undo, hold down right click to undo further. For keyboard use the &quot;z&quot; key, and for Xbox controllers use the B button.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The settings menu is in the top left, allowing you to adjust volume, reset the game, hide the UI, or quit.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Taking inspiration from The Witness, Tunic, and many other great games, Gordian is a finely crafted puzzle game full of tricks and secrets.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Tie all 21 knots as tight as possible in order to learn about topology through the rule set Gordian uses to represent it.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Click to place rope, and then click circles to move it to adjacent tiles.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Right click to undo your last move, hold to undo more.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Earn medals by tying knots as tight as possible, which unlocks more knots for you to puzzle over.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This game can be quite a challenge at times. If you find yourself overwhelmed, your brain tied into knots, just set the game down for a bit. Don't worry, it will save your progress.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Take your time. Before you know it your brain will be solving knots in the background and you'll come back with a whole new perspective.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Controls:</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Click anywhere place the first dot, from there you may extend the rope in any of the indicated directions by clicking (or tapping) in a valid location.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Right click to undo, hold down right click to undo further. For keyboard use the &quot;z&quot; key, and for Xbox controllers use the B button.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The settings menu is in the top left, allowing you to adjust volume, reset the game, hide the UI, or quit.</p>",
    "short_description": "A mix between perspective and spacial understanding, Gordian tasks you with translating knots diagrams to a hexagonal grid. Chill vibes, difficult puzzles, and a first of it's kind knot detection system. Chase scores or get creative, tie the knot in Gordian!",
